# =============================================================
# ANVATION 2026 — Local app configuration
# =============================================================
# === BACKEND RUNTIME ===
# Keep these values on the backend host only. Never prefix them with VITE_.
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3001
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:password@localhost:5432/anvation
SESSION_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-value
ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD=change-me-before-running-production
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3001

# This project is fully self-contained and does not require a remote API key.
#
# === SMTP EMAIL DELIVERY (REQUIRED to actually mail participants) ===
# Out of the box the server only generates a downloadable .eml file and does
# NOT deliver real mail. To send the Registration Confirmation (with the
# Gate Entry Pass QR and each participant's college) to the leader's and
# members' inboxes, provide a working SMTP account:
#
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com        # e.g. Gmail, Outlook, Zoho, Yandex, etc.
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_SECURE=false               # true for port 465
# SMTP_USER=your-account@gmail.com
# SMTP_PASS=your-app-password     # Gmail: use an App Password, not the login pass
# MAIL_FROM="Anvation 2026 <your-account@gmail.com>"
#
# Gmail SMTP requires an App Password (https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords)
# after enabling 2-Step Verification. Google may otherwise reject the login.
#
# Copy this file to a local `.env` file (same folder as server.ts), fill in your
# SMTP credentials, and restart:  npm run dev
#
# === OPTIONAL — VERTICAL SCALING / MULTI-CORE (for high traffic) ===
# The site already runs a single process which reliably handles thousands of
# concurrent visitors thanks to built-in compression, immutable asset caching
# and rate limiting (all enabled by default). To also use every CPU core on the
# server, set the number of worker processes:
#
# CLUSTER_WORKERS=auto     # "auto" = all logical cores minus 1, or set a number
# CLUSTER_WORKERS=8
#
# In cluster mode the server runs one authoritative process (which owns all
# data + API logic on a private loopback port, see INTERNAL_PORT) plus N worker
# processes that share the public port and serve static assets & proxy API
# calls to the authority. Registration/check-in data stays consistent and the
# file store is never duplicated. Interal port can be changed if 3002 is taken:
#
# INTERNAL_PORT=3002        # private loopback port used by cluster workers
#
# Cluster mode is experimental in Node and gracefully falls back to the single
# process if it cannot start, so it is safe to enable.
#
# === OPTIONAL — RATE LIMITING / SECURITY (already sensible by default) ===
# A global per-IP API throttle (300 req/min) and a stricter auth/email throttle
# (20 req/min) are active out of the box. Place the server behind a reverse
# proxy + TLS (nginx/caddy) and it will automatically trust X-Forwarded-For so
# each visitor is rate-limited individually.

# === OPTIONAL — PUSH THE CSV BACKUP TO GITHUB ===
# Disabled unless explicitly enabled. The server must run inside a writable Git
# clone with an SSH deploy key or credential helper already configured. Never
# put a GitHub token or private key in this file or in the repository.
#
# GITHUB_BACKUP_SYNC=true
# GITHUB_BACKUP_REPO_DIR=/opt/anvation
# GITHUB_BACKUP_RELATIVE_PATH=backups/participant-registration-backup.csv
# GITHUB_BACKUP_REMOTE=origin
# GITHUB_BACKUP_BRANCH=main
# GITHUB_BACKUP_AUTHOR_NAME=ANVATION Backup Bot
# GITHUB_BACKUP_AUTHOR_EMAIL=anvation-backup@users.noreply.github.com
